1
00:00:04,471 --> 00:00:10,247
This is the NOGUM App. Let’s set up a game of cosmic horror, from start to finish.

2
00:00:10,510 --> 00:00:15,479
We pick NOGUM Accelerated: the essentials, to play this very evening.

3
00:00:15,744 --> 00:00:21,935
First, the universe. Do you have a known one in mind?

4
00:00:22,204 --> 00:00:26,604
A present-day world, with mystery…

5
00:00:26,872 --> 00:00:31,727
…and the frightening kind: elder gods, forbidden books and madness.

6
00:00:31,996 --> 00:00:38,385
Two clicks, and the table already knows what fits in its world and how big its feats can be.

7
00:00:38,652 --> 00:00:44,548
Now, the tone. No technical questions: just situations, and you say what you expect.

8
00:00:44,814 --> 00:00:51,820
A good climber, in no hurry, with good gear. What does the table expect? That the wall takes its toll.

9
00:00:52,084 --> 00:00:58,474
A noise at the end of the corridor to distract the guard. He looks… without quite buying it.

10
00:00:58,740 --> 00:01:04,599
Is luck on your side? In Innsmouth, no.

11
00:01:04,868 --> 00:01:09,509
The universe puts you to the test. It’s settled: a hostile tone.

12
00:01:09,775 --> 00:01:16,167
Chaos. Three sessions planning a heist… and it half works. Neither Swiss watch nor roulette.

13
00:01:16,432 --> 00:01:22,509
A tavern brawl with nothing at stake: luck picks the winner, and two chairs get broken.

14
00:01:22,774 --> 00:01:33,228
Do plans go wrong where nobody was looking? No need. This atmosphere isn’t chaotic: it’s oppressive.

15
00:01:33,494 --> 00:01:41,698
Hostile, and no chaos: Terror mode. Before a single die is rolled, the table already knows how it will feel holding them.

16
00:01:41,969 --> 00:01:47,363
That’s the table. All of it fits in a short Code you share with the players.

17
00:01:47,631 --> 00:01:58,114
Now, an investigator. A new sheet comes out of the template sheet.

18
00:01:58,383 --> 00:02:02,350
Frank Delaney, private detective. Boston, 1927.

19
00:02:02,612 --> 00:02:08,967
Fourteen points. He knows how to investigate, look twice and read what he shouldn’t…

20
00:02:09,229 --> 00:02:18,323
…move without a sound, get the truth out of a witness and, if there’s no other way, pull the trigger.

21
00:02:18,586 --> 00:02:28,715
Gear belongs to whoever carries it. Search by name, or by what it does.

22
00:02:28,981 --> 00:02:33,013
A camera, for what nobody would believe without proof…

23
00:02:33,279 --> 00:02:37,879
…and a small revolver. In case the proof comes looking for him.

24
00:02:38,148 --> 00:02:43,178
The bill. In Accelerated, gear only costs money: and he can afford it.

25
00:02:43,449 --> 00:02:50,060
Whatever isn’t on the list is written in by hand: a black-covered notebook.

26
00:02:50,330 --> 00:03:01,180
The campaign’s memory lives in Story. First, where Frank comes from.

27
00:03:01,448 --> 00:03:10,215
And the campaign, already written: The Shadow over Innsmouth.

28
00:03:10,483 --> 00:03:17,070
The Questions tab answers from what’s written here. And the GM’s secret, under lock if need be.

29
00:03:17,339 --> 00:03:25,213
And now, play. Frank checks into the Gilman House hotel and listens through the wall.

30
00:03:25,482 --> 00:03:30,891
Terror mode: only the red die counts.
